    [
        'id'=>'cse-clerical-records-filing-and-proofreading','board'=>'civil-service','subject'=>'clerical-ability','title'=>'Civil Service Clerical Ability: Filing, Exact Comparison, and Proofreading','pdf'=>'cse-clerical-records-filing-and-proofreading.pdf',
        'scope'=>['csc-cse-ppt-scope-2026'],'instruction'=>['purdue-owl-grammar','purdue-owl-proofreading-errors'],
        'scope_note'=>'CSC scope materials include clerical ability at the Subprofessional level, particularly filing and spelling. This guide develops careful comparison and record-control habits; consult the current CSC announcement for the examination level and scope.',
        'objectives'=>['Apply one stated alphabetizing rule consistently.','Compare records character by character without silently correcting the source.','Proofread spelling and common sentence errors in context.'],
        'sections'=>[
            ['id'=>'filing-order-and-index-keys','heading'=>'1. Filing order starts with the filing key','body'=>'First identify the rule the question supplies: surname, organization name, title, or a specified filing code. Compare the first filing unit, then move character by character to the first difference. If the initial strings match, the shorter complete key normally precedes the longer one unless the stated local rule says otherwise. Treat spaces, punctuation, initials, and suffixes according to the instructions rather than inventing a convention. When an office uses a particular filing standard, follow that documented standard and record the key used so the order can be repeated.','concepts'=>['cse-filing','cse-filing-system-selection','cse-alphabetical-order']],
            ['id'=>'exact-record-comparison','heading'=>'2. Compare two records without guessing','body'=>'An exact comparison asks whether two strings or records match, not whether they probably refer to the same person. Compare fields in a stable order: identifier, name, date, address, and document version. Mark the first differing character or field, then check whether the task expects exact identity, a likely match, or a spelling correction. Preserve the source value until the responsible record owner authorizes a correction. This distinction prevents a near match from being filed as a confirmed duplicate and keeps the audit trail visible.','concepts'=>['cse-record-comparison']],
            ['id'=>'spelling-and-proofreading','heading'=>'3. Spelling and proofreading in context','body'=>'Proofreading works best in deliberate passes. Read once for meaning and missing words, once for spelling and word forms, and once for punctuation or repeated material. Check a doubtful spelling against a trusted dictionary or the supplied reference; do not rely only on the visual shape of a familiar word. Context can distinguish homophones and inflected forms, but a sentence should not be “corrected” by changing its intended meaning. In clerical work, accuracy also includes reproducing names, numbers, and source wording exactly when transcription is required.','concepts'=>['cse-spelling','cse-proofreading']],
        ],
        'examples'=>[['heading'=>'Alphabetize a small file list','prompt'=>'Which surname comes first alphabetically: Salazar, Santiago, Santos, or Sarmiento?','steps'=>['Compare the common prefix “Sa.”','Compare the next letters: Salazar has “l”; the other names have “n” or “r.”','Since “l” precedes “n” and “r,” Salazar is first.'],'answer'=>'Salazar.','check'=>'Do not compare the first name until the filing surname is resolved.']],
        'misconceptions'=>['A familiar name should be sorted by first name even when the key is surname.','Near-identical records can be treated as duplicates without checking identifiers.','Proofreading means improving the wording even when the task requires exact copying.'],
        'patterns'=>['Write the filing key before comparing entries.','Mark the first exact difference in two records.','Separate correction from faithful transcription.'],
        'questions'=>[['id'=>'692','section'=>'filing-order-and-index-keys','concept'=>'cse-filing','sources'=>['csc-cse-ppt-scope-2026','purdue-owl-proofreading-errors']]],
